#: src/components/Welcome.tsx:49
msgid "<0>A promise about what this is:</0> Grove is not a records race. No hint leaves, no completeness meters, no \"12,000 people in your tree!\". Dates are scaffolding; what the family <1>remembers</1> about a person is the point. Start with one name and let it grow at the pace of remembering."
msgstr ""

#: src/components/HelpSheet.tsx:109
msgid "<0>Family name at birth</0> is for a maiden name, or any family name that changed later. It shows on their page as <1>born …</1>."
msgstr ""

#: src/components/HelpSheet.tsx:214
msgid "<0>Guardians</0> — a few people you trust who can jointly let you back in. You tell each of them a codeword out loud. No single guardian, and no server, ever holds your key."
msgstr ""

#: src/components/HelpSheet.tsx:271
msgid "<0>Import a .ged</0> brings in a tree from elsewhere. It only ever adds — it never overwrites what's here, and it won't try to merge people who look alike."
msgstr ""

#: src/components/HelpSheet.tsx:221
msgid "<0>Quick unlock</0> uses this device's fingerprint or face in place of typing. It's a convenience for one device; the passphrase stays the real key."
msgstr ""

#: src/components/HelpSheet.tsx:173
msgid "<0>See the tree</0>, or <1>In the tree</1> on anyone's page, draws the family around one person: those they came from above, those who came from them below, partners alongside on a dashed line."
msgstr ""

#: src/components/HelpSheet.tsx:35
msgid "<0>Share</0> plants a tree the family tends together. It travels through an account, so connect <1>Sync</1> first. Then invite people by an email address you already know, or make an invite link — good for 7 days or 20 uses — and send it somewhere you'd trust with the family's story."
msgstr ""

#: src/components/HelpSheet.tsx:139
msgid "<0>What it says, typed out</0> is worth the few minutes. Handwriting fades and is hard to read on a phone; typed words can be read aloud, translated, and carried to other genealogy tools when you export. The scan stays as the proof; the words become the memory."
msgstr ""

